<!--
  Commander Battle's troop classes, merged into Native's mpclassdivisions.xml (MPClassDivisions, MultiplayerGame only).
  - One class per weight of a formation class (role): infantry heavy/medium/light, ranged light/heavy, cavalry
    heavy/medium/light... The weight label comes from the multiplier bands per role (CommanderRoles.WeightBands).
  - A culture's first 7 classes take over its 7 stock class ids in place (_replaceWhileMerging="true"), so they keep the
    stock index (MissionPeer.SelectedTroopIndex) and every class of the culture is ours. Further classes get new cb_ ids
    and are appended. Never put _replaceWhileMerging on a NEW id: with no id match the merger replaces the FIRST class
    of the file instead (MBObjectManager.MergeElements).
  - At most 16 classes per culture (the troop index is 4 bits).
  - multiplier: the class's size weight. A formation fields budget x ceil(100 x multiplier) / the average of its role's
    classes, so it only compares within a role.
  - The only perk list (perk_list="1") is the weapon setups. Index 0 is the class's own loadout; the others swap weapon
    slots with AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn (target Any: commander and troops). No TroopCountOnSpawn: only the weight sets
    the count. game_mode="all": the server's GameType is CommanderBattle, so stock "Captain" perks would never apply.
    AI-led formations get a setup too (MissionMultiplayerCommanderBattle.AssignDefaultClasses).
  - Setups are in the order of the culture variance pass (docs/plans/troop-types.md): the AI fields setup k for its k-th
    formation of a role. A setup for medium and heavy only is simply absent from the light class.
  - Two-handed and pike setups carry no shield: the shield slot (Item1) is cleared by an AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn
    without item (AlternativeEquipmentEffect.Deserialize sets an empty element).
  - Sidearm (Item2) rule: spears, pikes and lances keep the culture's sidearm, since they fight poorly up close.
    Swords, axes and maces, and swung two-handers (bill, voulge), clear it: their main weapon already is one.
  - A bad node makes the loader drop every later entry of this file silently; the CommanderBattle log lists the
    classes per culture when a mission opens.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml (the only items multiplayer loads).
-->
